Description: peer-to-peer voice and text chat for the terminal
 tincan opens a chat room in the terminal, reached by room name and
 passphrase or by an invite code. A room has text channels and voice, with
 Opus audio, noise suppression, push-to-talk and a choice of microphone and
 speaker. Voice is optional: without a working audio device the session
 carries on as text only.
 .
 Peers find each other and get through NAT with iroh's default n0
 infrastructure, public relay servers and a DNS discovery service that n0
 runs, which also relay the encrypted traffic when no direct path can be
 made. A room cannot open, or be joined, without reaching them.
 .
 The invite code is copied to the clipboard when wl-copy, xclip or xsel is
 installed.
